    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0702" n="610" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg610"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 103.94/507</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-02T13:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 2, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2.45 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2404. For Baruch from Summers:</p>
                <p>Your 1693, September 29 [<hi rendition="#italic">28</hi>], my 2369 of October 1.
                    At meeting Maritime Transport Council to-day Secretary Baker definitely
                    committed the United States to fully disclose its shipping programme, its import
                    programme and its programmes of all kinds.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d532-f1"/>
                    Understand the President authorized this. Suggest therefore that effort be made
                    to supply information through our programme committees rather than through other
                    sources.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
